      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The student's argument is fundamentally flawed because it treats national identity as a static, natural force rather than a constructed political tool used to exclude outsiders and justify inequality. Prioritizing nationalism over global integration often leads to the erosion of human rights and the suppression of minority voices within the very nations it claims to protect. Instead of fostering true social cohesion, this approach frequently creates internal divisions and fuels xenophobia by defining \"us\" against \"them.\" A more robust perspective recognizes that global cooperation and shared human values are the only sustainable foundations for a just and cohesive society.",
